From: Benoit Masson <yahoo@perenite.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: bridge aware path checks

Two accept checks compare against the device a frame arrives on or
leaves through, and both assume that device is also the one the FIB
names. Behind a software bridge it is not: the FIB names the bridge,
a bridge does not rewrite the source of frames it forwards, and routed
traffic carries the bridge address out of a member port.

The IPv6 source-route check then always failed (the FIB resolves the
source through the bridge while the ingress is a member), declining
every routed IPv6 flow; the egress source check rejected the correct
bridge address the flowtable offered, declining routed IPv6 in the
other direction as well. Both print once per reason, so the flows
looked silently software.

Compare against the bridge master in both places. DSA setups are
unaffected: a conduit and its user ports share one address, so the
master comparison was already true there.

Measured on TP-Link Archer BE800 (IPQ9574, ports under a software
bridge, no DSA): routed IPv6 offloads both directions at 2.32 Gbit/s
with the CPU port seeing 226 packets per 15 s transfer, against the
full line rate in software before; IPv4 NAT unchanged at 9 CPU packets
per transfer.

Signed-off-by: Benoit Masson <yahoo@perenite.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c	2026-10-02 08:00:46.550002523 +0000
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c	2026-10-02 08:00:46.560002523 +0000
@@ -940,6 +940,16 @@
 	return true;
 }
 
+/* Routed traffic egressing a bridge member keeps the bridge MAC as
+ * source (a bridge does not rewrite it), so the valid egress source MAC
+ * is the member address or that of its master.
+ */
+static const u8 *ppe_offload_egress_l3_mac(struct net_device *dev)
+{
+	struct net_device *master = netdev_master_upper_dev_get(dev);
+
+	return master ? master->dev_addr : dev->dev_addr;
+}
+
 static int ppe_offload_flow_replace(struct net_device *netdev,
 				     struct ppe_offload_priv *priv,
 				     struct flow_cls_offload *cls)
@@ -1201,7 +1211,7 @@
 			dst_on_ingress = __ip_dev_find(dev_net(netdev), match_dst, false) == l3dev;
 		if (l3dev && ipv6)
 			src_via_ingress = ppe_offload_ipv6_reached_via(dev_net(netdev), &match_src6,
-								       l3dev);
+				netdev_master_upper_dev_get_rcu(idev) ? : l3dev);
 	}
 	if (idev)
 		idev = ppe_offload_ingress_edma_dev(idev);
@@ -1451,7 +1461,9 @@
 	 * Behind a DSA user port that is the conduit's MAC, which its
 	 * user ports and (by default) their bridge inherit.
 	 */
-	if (!ether_addr_equal(eth.bytes + ETH_ALEN, egress.dev->dev_addr))
+	if (!ether_addr_equal(eth.bytes + ETH_ALEN, egress.dev->dev_addr) &&
+	    !ether_addr_equal(eth.bytes + ETH_ALEN,
+			      ppe_offload_egress_l3_mac(egress.dev)))
 		return ppe_offload_decline("eth mangle src %pM != egress %s mac %pM",
 					    eth.bytes + ETH_ALEN, netdev_name(egress.dev),
 					    egress.dev->dev_addr);
